      "math_academy_id": "q-37962",
      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}-4x+\\phantom{1}0\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,3{x}^{2}-4x+0 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,3{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5x+15}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,15\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$-term and the constant term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}-4x+0\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-3x+5 \\\\  & x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}-4x+\\phantom{1}0\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,3{x}^{2}-4x+0 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,3{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x+0 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5x+15}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}-3x+5\\,$ and $\\,5x+0.$",
